--- body ---
## Context

Child of tickets/0205 (external-reviewer panel). GitHub Copilot code
review = cross-vendor reviewer at zero token cost, server-side, async.
Subscription confirmed (author, 2026-06-04). Copilot comments but never
approves, so any "required" semantics are enforced as a verify-gate
disposition precondition, never a forge approval rule.

Author decision (2026-07-13): **on-demand, not auto-request**. Repo-wide
auto-request reviews every merge request, including trivial ones — waste
of review latency and noise. The Copilot seat is requested per-PR, by
the author or by the reviewer-panel tooling, when the change warrants
outside eyes. No forge-side auto-request lever is enabled.

## Relevant files

- skills/reviewers/SKILL.md — the request verb: add a Copilot seat to
  a given PR on demand (per-PR reviewer request via the forge API;
  document the exact mechanism in this ticket's log)
- skills/gaze/SKILL.md — gate-inputs clause (harvest when present)
- tickets/0205 — contract + observation-period definition

## Actions

1. On-demand request path: /reviewers can request a Copilot review on
   a named PR (forge API reviewer request; document the exact call in
   this ticket's log). No repo setting, no ruleset — nothing fires
   without an explicit request.
2. skills/gaze/SKILL.md gate clause: the comment-validation step
   includes "the forge's automated reviewer, when present" — findings
   dispositioned like any panel comment; correctness-class only may
   bounce, style is noted-not-blocking. A PR with no Copilot review is
   simply a PR without that seat — no warning, no wait. Only when a
   request WAS made and is still pending: bounded wait (few minutes),
   then proceed with a logged WARN — fail-open.
   GitHub-specific mechanics carry <!-- harness-extension-point -->.
3. Advisory trial per 0205: request the seat on at least 5 non-trivial
   merge requests across at least 3 projects; log a one-line scorecard
   per MR (findings, true/false positives) in this ticket.

## Test

First MR of the trial shows a requested-and-harvested Copilot comment
dispositioned in the gate verdict's evidence table.

## Exit criteria

- [x] On-demand request path live; exact forge call documented
- [x] Gate clause merged (absent seat is silent; requested-but-pending
      gets fail-open bounded wait)
- [ ] Trial scorecard: ≥5 non-trivial MRs, ≥3 projects, logged here
- [ ] Promote/drop recommendation recorded for 0205's integration review
